    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0316" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2129</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania, Servia, and Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-14T17:00:00+01:44">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 14, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 17, 7.42 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. It is believed an agreement has been signed between Bulgaria and Turkey and
                    that a German-Austrian army will shortly attack Servia in which case it is
                    believed that Roumania will join Servia. Roumania is prepared for war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
